2026-07-30 PR #32 (0 -> 160, 160 more row(s)): Bootstrap the initial known-diff list for the new swetest text-diff harness.
2026-07-30 PR #32 (160 -> 150, 10 fewer row(s)): Fixed eight pointer-arithmetic-as-string-concatenation crash sites (int.Parse/C.atof/string-assign taking argv[i]+N as concatenation instead of an offset substring), the -house %c sscanf InvalidCastException, and the -utc Substring(4,30) ArgumentOutOfRangeException. All 11 known CRASH rows resolve: 10 now match the C reference exactly and are pruned; CRASH_MISC|AY no longer crashes but exposes a pre-existing, unrelated output difference (missing ayanamsha name in the Ayanamsha line) now visible because the crash no longer masks it.
2026-07-30 PR #32 (150 -> 150, no change in row count): Force -edir absolute (Resolve-EpheDir) so the port cannot silently fall back to Moshier via a relative ephemeris path, and add Test-RequiredFileMissReported: a hard failure when either binary reports a required, already-confirmed-present ephemeris file as not found on an -eswe row. Investigation (manual repro against Programs/SweTest/bin/Release/net10.0/SweTest.exe and external/.c-reference/swetest.exe) confirmed the defect is real -- a relative -edir gives Sun 279.8584626 and 'using Moshier eph.' on the .NET side against 279.8584613 (matching the C reference) with an absolute -edir -- but that this harness's own default EpheDir was already an absolute, Resolve-Path-derived value from its first commit onward, so none of the 150 previously tracked rows were actually measured against a degraded ephemeris; the fix closes the caller-override path that could have reintroduced it and adds the guard that would have caught it.
2026-07-30 PR #32 (150 -> 143, 7 fewer row(s)): Phase 4 slice A fixed rot_back's J2000 obliquity, which nothing in this port ever populated, so every planetary position computed from an ephemeris file moved toward the C. 87 of 230 cases now match byte for byte, up from 80.
2026-07-31 PR #32 (143 -> 152, 9 more row(s)): Port swetest.c 2.10.03 (99 hunks) and swemini.c (2 hunks): -cob/-pc/-lim/-ep/-tpm/-sidbit/-dh/-xv, m/z format letters, -utc short form; grid grown from 230 to 252 rows to cover the new surface
2026-07-31 PR #32 (152 -> 152, no change in row count): Scrub the repo root and ephemeris directory to stable placeholders before a reason is written, and make the truncation anchor on the first differing character instead of the shared prefix, so a regenerate is reproducible across checkouts and a long common-prefix row still shows what differs
2026-07-31 PR #32 (152 -> 152, no change in row count): Second run to confirm the regenerate is byte-identical across runs (reproducibility check for the path-scrubbing fix)
2026-07-31 PR #32 (152 -> 152, no change in row count): Restore LF line endings after a git stash/pop round-trip (used only to diff against a temp copy while verifying this fix) let core.autocrlf convert the file to CRLF; row content unaffected, confirmed byte-identical to the prior run before the round-trip
2026-07-31 PR #32 (152 -> 47, 105 fewer row(s)): dms() had the leading space on the opposite branch from both C versions (swetest.c:2688 is sprintf(s, " %3d%s", kdeg, c)). Restoring it fixes an ArgumentOutOfRangeException once a value reached 100 degrees and closes the one-column padding gap in every degree-bearing field.
2026-07-31 PR #32 (47 -> 24, 23 fewer row(s)): hms() 8-char truncation (swetest.c:3937), sout append at :3204, and the BIT_ZODIAC format+sign-insertion fix (swetest.c:2686/:2723-2725) close the ECLIPSE and ORBEL known-diff families and fix FMT_LETTERS|Z.
2026-07-31 PR #32 (24 -> 21, 3 fewer row(s)): SE_VERSION bumped from 2.08 to 2.10.03; the three HEADER_BLOCK PORT-VERSION rows were a pure version-banner difference and now match since both binaries report 2.10.03.
2026-08-01 PR #32 (21 -> 15, 6 fewer row(s)): The 2b default-path fix closed these six: each recorded divergence was the ephemeris path in swetest's own output, c="PATH '\sweph\ephe\'" against net="PATH '[ephe]'". Resolving upstream's real default by OS at run time (01074be) makes both sides agree, so the rows now match outright.
2026-08-01 PR #32 (15 -> 12, 3 fewer row(s)): Fix SweTest -p<seq> single-char truncation (char vs char* divergence from swetest.c:1120) and add a Gauquelin (-houseN,N,G) grid case exercising the cusp[37] out-of-bounds read that swetest.c:1958-1959 performs as benign stack UB and the port previously threw on
